# Ignore all files in Temp except Temp/SConscript
Temp/*
!Temp/SConscript

vc140.pdb
.sconsign.dblite
RetroXR/libretro-godot/~*
# MSVC build artifacts (generated alongside the DLL, not needed at runtime)
RetroXR/libretro-godot/*.exp
RetroXR/libretro-godot/*.ilk
RetroXR/libretro-godot/*.lib
RetroXR/libretro-godot/*.pdb

# godot-pdfium build artifacts
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/~*
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/*.exp
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/*.ilk
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/*.lib
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/*.pdb
godot-pdfium/Temp/
godot-pdfium/external/pdfium/include/*.orig

# vlc-godot build artifacts
RetroXR/vlc-godot/~*
RetroXR/vlc-godot/*.exp
RetroXR/vlc-godot/*.ilk
RetroXR/vlc-godot/*.lib
RetroXR/vlc-godot/*.pdb

# .import sidecars are tracked, not ignored. They hold each asset's import
# settings (the system icons' svg/scale=0.5, the bedroom NormalGL maps'
# compress/normal_map=1) and its uid://, which .tscn and .tres reference by
# UID rather than by path. A clone that regenerates them invents different
# UIDs and re-derives every setting from defaults. The build output they point
# at lives in .godot/, which is ignored above.

*.apk

# Godot-specific ignores
.import/
export.cfg

# export_presets.cfg is deliberately NOT ignored. Godot 4.5+ keeps keystore paths,
# keystore passwords and the script encryption key in RetroXR/.godot/export_credentials.cfg,
# which RetroXR/.gitignore excludes as part of .godot/, so the preset carries no secrets.

# Imported translations (automatically generated from CSV files)
*.translation

# Mono-specific ignores
.mono/
data_*/
mono_crash.*.json

# Blender-specific ignores
*.blend[0-9]*

# Local libretro core root. On Linux default_core_root() is $HOME/retroxr/libretro,
# which lands inside the repo when it's cloned at ~/retroxr. Never commit cores.
/libretro/

/roms/
/dvd/
/books/
/audio/
/videos/
/music/

# metaxr-audio build artifacts (same convention as libretro-godot / godot-pdfium)
RetroXR/metaxr-audio/~*
RetroXR/metaxr-audio/*.exp
RetroXR/metaxr-audio/*.ilk
RetroXR/metaxr-audio/*.lib
RetroXR/metaxr-audio/*.pdb
metaxr-audio/Temp/

# Output of RetroXR/Tools/bedroom_probe.tscn — renders, never source.
RetroXR/probe_out/
# Tools/bios_boot_survey.sh output: per-attempt logs and the options snapshot
bios_survey_out/
*.mp4

# Audio .import files carry compress/mode=0 — QOA-compressed clips cannot be
# decoded to PCM frames for the Meta XR emitter, so the setting must ship.
!RetroXR/Audio/**/*.import

# verlet-rope build artifacts (same convention as libretro-godot / vlc-godot)
RetroXR/verlet-rope/~*
RetroXR/verlet-rope/*.exp
RetroXR/verlet-rope/*.ilk
RetroXR/verlet-rope/*.lib
RetroXR/verlet-rope/*.pdb
verlet-rope/Temp/

# archive-godot build artifacts
RetroXR/archive-godot/~*
RetroXR/archive-godot/*.exp
RetroXR/archive-godot/*.ilk
RetroXR/archive-godot/*.lib
RetroXR/archive-godot/*.pdb
archive-godot/Temp/
vlc-godot/Temp/

# ── Compiled GDExtensions ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────
# Our own six libraries are BUILD OUTPUT and are not carried in the repo — run
# `python Tools/build.py <platform>` to produce them. They were tracked until
# 2026-08-02 and cost ~267 MB of history between them, most of it the same debug
# binary recommitted on every rebuild (the Android debug .so alone had 37
# versions). See the Building section of the README.
#
# Matched by our own naming only. Everything else in those directories is
# third-party runtime that MUST stay tracked: SDL3.dll, libvlc/libvlccore and the
# VLC plugin tree, pdfium, and the Meta XR Audio blob. libvlc.so in particular is
# not just shipped — vlc-godot's Android build LINKS against it out of that
# directory, so dropping it would break the build outright.
# The leading `*` is load-bearing: the Linux libretro build emits a bare
# `libretro_godot.linux…so` with no lib prefix, where every other target emits
# `lib<name>…so`. `*name.` matches both, since `*` also matches nothing.
RetroXR/libretro-godot/*libretro_godot.*.dll
RetroXR/libretro-godot/*libretro_godot.*.so
RetroXR/libretro-godot/*libretro_godot.*.dylib
RetroXR/archive-godot/*archive_godot.*.dll
RetroXR/archive-godot/*archive_godot.*.so
RetroXR/archive-godot/*archive_godot.*.dylib
RetroXR/verlet-rope/*verlet_rope.*.dll
RetroXR/verlet-rope/*verlet_rope.*.so
RetroXR/verlet-rope/*verlet_rope.*.dylib
RetroXR/vlc-godot/*vlc_godot.*.dll
RetroXR/vlc-godot/*vlc_godot.*.so
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/*godot-pdfium.*.dll
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/*godot-pdfium.*.so
RetroXR/godot-pdfium/*godot-pdfium.*.dylib
RetroXR/metaxr-audio/*metaxr-audio.*.dll
RetroXR/metaxr-audio/*metaxr-audio.*.so

# Windows ReplaceFile() backups. The Win32 call that swaps a file in place leaves
# the old copy behind as `~<name>~RF<hex>.TMP`, and something re-writes the OpenXR
# vendors DLL on most editor runs — four had piled up in .bin/windows/, each a
# byte-identical 5 MB copy of libgodotopenxrvendors.dll.
#
# Deliberately narrow: the RF<hex> form is unmistakably that API's, where a blanket
# *.TMP could hide a real artefact. The DLL these shadow must STAY tracked — a
# missing Windows binary makes Godot drop the whole GDExtension, which once
# shipped a Quest APK with no vendors .so and no passthrough.
~*~RF*.TMP

# Claude Code machine-local settings (absolute paths, per-machine allow-list)
.claude/settings.local.json

# Its own repo, cloned beside the tools that build its core.
Tools/azahar-libretro-vr/

.claude/worktrees/

# Mods authored in this checkout (Tools/mods/new_mod.py). Never ours to ship:
# an author works in RetroXR/mods/<id>/ so their scenes resolve against the real
# classes and uids, then packs from there. Also excluded from the export presets.
RetroXR/mods/

.desloppify/
